WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.925
Here is the learning path for Module 4 We are going
to

00:00:03.938 --> 00:00:07.388
build the ideas gradually so that each new concept
connects to something

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:13.162
you already understand First we summarize You will
work with COUNT

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:18.738
SUM AVG MIN and MAX These functions take several
input rows and

00:00:18.762 --> 00:00:24.275
calculate a summary value Second we group GROUP BY
lets us

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:29.362
create a separate summary for each category or
combination of categories For

00:00:29.375 --> 00:00:32.725
example instead of one total for the whole sales
table we can

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:38.575
calculate one total per product category Third we
filter WHERE

00:00:38.588 --> 00:00:42.862
and HAVING both remove data but they work at
different stages WHERE

00:00:42.875 --> 00:00:48.212
removes source rows before aggregation HAVING
removes groups after the aggregates have

00:00:48.225 --> 00:00:53.775
been calculated Understanding that difference will
make many analytical queries much easier

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:59.688
to reason about Finally we extend the analysis We
will build conditional

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:03.875
metrics create multiple levels of totals and use
window functions for ranking

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:09.100
averages and running totals without losing detail
rows The coding progression is

00:01:09.112 --> 00:01:13.225
the same beginner-friendly pattern we used earlier
run a complete example change

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:16.612
one piece complete a partially written query and
then write a short

00:01:16.638 --> 00:01:22.425
query yourself The goal is not memorization The goal
is to understand

00:01:22.438 --> 00:01:23.938
the reasoning behind the query
